#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# hilbert_transform

#% text
# `hilbert_transform(f, t, s)` gives the Hilbert transform `(1/pi) PV integrate(f(t)/(s - t), [t, -inf, inf])`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# By linearity from the transforms of `sin(a t + b)`, `cos(a t + b)`, `exp(im (a t + b))`, `dirac_delta(t)` and constants, and for a rational function vanishing at infinity from its complex partial fractions: `(t - z)^-k` becomes `im sign(im(z)) (s - z)^-k`.

#% item
# A numeric s evaluates the closed form at s.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
hilbert_transform(sin(t), t, s)
#% output
#= -cos(s)

#% cell
hilbert_transform(1/(1 + t^2), t, s)
#% output
#= s/(1 + s^2)

#% cell
hilbert_transform(exp(2*im*t), t, s)
#% output
#= -im*exp(2im*s)

#% cell
hilbert_transform(dirac_delta(t), t, s)
#% output
#= 1/(pi*s)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `inverse_hilbert_transform`, `fourier_transform`
